+# HWM IKV deployment and experimental modes
+
+The default `ikv.history_mode: off` keeps the original inference path. Enabling IKV requires the sibling `ikv_runtime` package on `PYTHONPATH` (or installed from its source) and real learned scorer assets. The scorer uses its own pinned Qwen3.5-0.8B encoder; it never shares weights or features with the native HWM Planner. There is no heuristic fallback when scorer files or revisions are incompatible.
+
+## Two independent switches
+
+Set these fields under `ikv` in `deploy.yml`:
+
+| `history_mode` | `planner_mode` | Behavior |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `window_refresh` | `lower_only` | Re-encode the original lower-model history window and the native Planner history. Score lower-model KV using the task alone. |
+| `incremental_reuse` | `lower_only` | Encode each new observation; reuse historical KV and cached native Planner image features. Planner history and semantic behavior remain native; lower KV scoring is task-only. |
+| `window_refresh` | `interactive` | Scorer retrieves historical head images for Planner; Planner freshly encodes those images. Updated subtask and semantic memory condition a second scorer call for lower KV. The lower native history window is independently refreshed. |
+| `incremental_reuse` | `interactive` | Same two-stage Planner/scorer interaction, reusing cached historical Planner image features and lower-model KV. Only new observations are encoded. |
+
+`incremental` is accepted as an alias for `incremental_reuse`, matching the DM05 side implementation's naming. Unlike DM05's same-format frame archive, HWM's two modes intentionally archive different native representations (packed temporal history versus current-head tokens), so switching modes requires an episode reset. `off` requires `planner_mode: lower_only`. The scorer's separate immutable image feature cache is used in both enabled history modes, but scores are recomputed using current context. `interactive` first uses the previous subtask/memory for coarse image retrieval, then the newly produced subtask/merged memory for fine KV scoring; it introduces no circular same-round dependency. Planner's learned WORLD/ACTION outputs still condition the model through its existing interfaces; they are not substituted for scorer encoder features.
+
+Example configuration (replace all three paths with actual assets):
+
+```yaml
+ikv:
+  history_mode: incremental_reuse
+  planner_mode: interactive
+  source_root: /path/to/scorer/source
+  checkpoint: /path/to/selected/scorer-head.pt
+  encoder_path: /path/to/pinned/Qwen3.5-0.8B
+  device: cuda:0
+  max_bytes: 68719476736
+  max_frames: 2048
+```
+
+Python callers may use `model.set_ikv_modes(history_mode="window_refresh", planner_mode="lower_only")`. Switching either axis resets all episode state. Restart client episodes at step zero after any mode change or server reset. An enabled mode cannot silently resume an episode for which the server has no archive.
+
+## What is retained and selected
+
+The lower-model historical capacity follows the original packing warmup: 0 slots for no history, 80 for 1–3 historical RGB observations, 160 for 4–7, 180 for 8–15, and 186 for 16–20. All current candidates and archived candidates are jointly scored; no arbitrary 80/106 protection split is imposed. Selection is a single stable ID plan across every layer. Missing rows are right-padded and masked, never counted as real observations.
+
+`window_refresh` archives actual pre-RoPE K/V at the native packed-history positions, including native spatial scales and temporal supports. Temporal VAE support metadata conservatively includes its causal RGB prefix. `incremental_reuse` instead archives each round's actual current-head K/V (80 positions) and later reads those as historical KV. It does not reconstruct old temporal VAE latents or run old historical queries. This is a different memory representation from native multi-frame history packing; it is not numerically equivalent to refreshing the original window. Deep historical states preserve the context in which they were created.
+
+Keys are stored before RoPE. Retrieval preserves each token's native spatial position and pooled complex frequency, shifting temporal phase into the current round's coordinates without assuming pooled RoPE has unit magnitude. The original directed mask remains in place: actions do not directly attend historical slots; history influences actions through video states. Selected KV are inserted before the first attention of the first denoising step and reused through that action chunk. Archive commits occur only after finite actions have been validated; failed inference aborts the KV transaction and does not publish semantic updates.
+
+## Native Planner image encoding
+
+In `incremental_reuse`, each new standalone head view is encoded and cached alongside that round's current three-camera mosaic. A head-only image and a mosaic crop do not have equivalent visual features. Old head features are then reused without re-encoding their RGB. The original Qwen language-model prompt/query prefill is still recomputed; this feature cache does not make the hybrid/recurrent Planner a persistent ordinary KV transformer.
+
+Strict current-only incremental operation requires `replan_steps` to equal the native history sampling interval (30 steps for this checkpoint), no skipped observation boundaries, and an episode starting at step zero. Otherwise unseen intermediate historical head frames could require old RGB encoding, so the implementation rejects the request. Window refresh supports the native configured replanning cadence.
+
+The updated `ContextClient` adds a stable client/slot identity for resetting server-side archives between episodes. Baseline ignores this additive field. RPC retries with identical inputs reuse the completed result; changed semantic context, state, or RGB under the same step is rejected. Legacy repeated `get_action` after its own committed semantic update also reuses the result.
+
+## Validation and limits
+
+CPU tests execute actual small HWM video/action DiT blocks, including first-step selection influence, per-layer archival, native-mask preservation, source position relocation, all native budget transitions, and transaction abort. The off path matches the original git source bitwise in these fixtures; selecting all fresh native members matches native output within numerical tolerance. Driver tests cover all four combinations, VAE/Planner cache routing, task-only versus interactive scoring, RPC/legacy replay, episode reset, and NaN rollback.
+
+Run from an environment with PyTorch, NumPy, Pillow and PyYAML:
+
+```bash
+PYTHONPATH=/path/to/ikv_runtime/parent:/path/to/HWM_0_preview \
+  python -m unittest discover -s /path/to/HWM_0_preview/tests -p 'test_hwm*.py' -v
+```
+
+These are code/integration tests, not full-checkpoint inference or RoboDojo results. The HWM checkpoint and its native Qwen/extension dependencies are still required. This adapter does not itself add pipeline-parallel weight partitioning. Full two-4090 PP loading, peak VRAM, latency and benchmark validation must be performed separately before running the requested evaluations.
+
+`max_bytes` caps archived K/V only. RGB and both encoders' feature caches are additional memory; `max_frames` is an explicit retention guard. The implementation fails rather than silently drop RGB still referenced by live archived KV. Archived image features and raw observations are episode-local and cleared on reset.
+
+
+## Canonical heuristic inference
+
+Set `ikv.backend: formula`, with `source_root` pointing to the current IKV
+core and `encoder_path` to verified raw DINOv3 assets. The new formula is the
+un-normalized sum of recency, visual contact decay and prototype-gated class
+recency, all weights one, threshold 0.75, decay 8 world/control steps. There
+is no random mixture. The bridge converts adapter seconds back to world steps
+explicitly (VPP2: 25 Hz; HWM: native control clock). DINO uses its own frozen
+encoder and maps its 14x14 scores to native KV provenance by area and temporal
+support. It does not share the Planner encoder.
+
+Native RGB-only requests have no contact-duration sidecar; their absent-contact
+value is d=0. The bridge accepts validated per-sensor contact durations (world
+steps) when a caller supplies them; it never guesses contact from RGB.
+Formula scoring has no instruction/subtask/semantic-memory term, so HWM formula
+runs require `planner_mode: lower_only`. Native Planner still runs normally.
+The learned backend retains its independent `interactive` option. Both history
+update modes remain available for formula runs. Feature caching and class-index
+reuse are episode-local and use only causal real observations. Prototype overflow
+fails explicitly rather than silently evicting classes.
